# Cloudflare Pages _redirects: minimal. Do NOT add SPA rewrites here.
#
# 2026-11-22 REGRESSION: adding functions/_middleware.js (ASSETS.fetch
# of /index.html) plus 200 rewrites for every SPA path broke the live
# site with ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS on /, /books, /speaking, /blog,
# /admin, /devotional and /index.html. Evidence from that deploy:
# /home loaded correctly with URL preserved, and /home had NO _redirects
# rule and NO middleware handling, so it fell through to Pages built-in
# SPA fallback, which serves index.html with the URL preserved. The
# paths WITH a 200 rewrite to /index.html loaded Home (Nov 19-22) or
# looped (Nov 22, with middleware). Conclusion: the 200 rewrites are
# the problem, not the client router. So this file now lists NO SPA
# path rewrites. Pages SPA fallback serves index.html for them.
# /api/* skips _redirects (Pages Functions). /assets/* is served directly.
# Keep only the sitemap self-rewrite so it is never caught by fallback.
/sitemap.xml /sitemap.xml 200
